        "original_id": "68d6fbc9-89d4-5225-93e3-34a20f020895",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Phelps, Klete Keller, Ryan Lochte, Peter Vanderkaay, Young Jeezy, Detail, Akon, Ray J, Lil Wayne, Beyoncé, Wiz Khalifa\n- Events: Athens games\n- Songs: \"I'm So Paid\", \"Sexy Can I\", \"How to Love\", \"Drunk in Love\", \"711\", \"We Dem Boyz\"\n- Topics: Olympic swimming, relay team, music references, record production\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Fred Phelps II was born on June 30, 1985.\n- Michael Phelps is an American former competitive swimmer and the most decorated Olympian of all time with 28 medals.\n- The American relay of Michael Phelps, Ryan Lochte, Peter Vanderkaay, and Klete Keller has been undefeated since the Athens games.\n- Young Jeezy's verse in the song \"I'm So Paid\" references fellow Olympian Michael Phelps.\n- Detail is known for producing hit singles including \"Sexy Can I\" by Ray J, \"I'm So Paid\" by Akon, \"How to Love\" by Lil Wayne, \"Drunk in Love\" and \"711\" by Beyoncé, and \"We Dem Boyz\" by Wiz Khalifa.",
